        "summary": "Agriculture is the foundational pillar of India's culture, economy, and rural employment. This chapter covers the historical journey of farming from ancient Harappan techniques to modern mechanised practices. It analyzes the close relationships between soil profiles, climatic rainfall patterns, water resources, and cropping seasons (Kharif, Rabi, Zaid), alongside the indispensable role of women in agriculture and sustainable farming methods.",
